<!--
    kuna x87depth: a discarded x87 call result makes a void function return
    `long double`.

    Source (gcc -m32 -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer):

        double g;
        double noisy(double x) { g = x; return x * 2; }
        void drop2(double x) { noisy(x); g += 1; }
        double keep(double x) { double a = noisy(x); double b = noisy(a + 1); return a * b; }

        80491b0 drop2: sub esp,4; push [esp+0xc]; push [esp+0xc]
        80491bb        call noisy          ; leaves its result in ST0
        80491c0        fstp st(0)          ; discards it
        80491c2        fld1
        80491c4        fadd qword [g]
        80491ca        fstp qword [g]      ; the x87 stack is empty again
        80491d0        add esp,0xc; ret

    SLEIGH has no x87 stack top: ST0..ST7 are fixed registers and each push or
    pop is a copy shift, and the call itself shifts nothing. At the `ret` ST0
    holds what the pops moved down, so return recovery finds a written ST0 and
    drop2 returns an undefined `long double`. The depth after the call is
    1 (the `fstp st(0)` pops a value), so it is 0 at the `ret`.

    Stage: P4 return recovery (ActionReturnRecovery, the x87emptyreturn drop),
    option x87depth off|on.  Pass 1 (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the
    default) the fix; keep, whose depth at its `ret` is 1, returns its value
    in both.
-->
